{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeexTQMLpRfZWdkgdZKw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate, **`running_tally_drift_ideal`**, and it passes the self-check (`OK`). Its fit is weak, though: the smoke fit's ELPD-LOO is about −1281, while the best model sits at −1070. That smoke fit is only 100 draws on one chain, so the real admission fit may differ. I didn't try to improve the fit.\n\n**Hypothesis:** As people read a sequence, they keep a running tally of how far heads lead tails. Each person expects a fair coin's tally to drift away from even by some typical amount. A sequence looks random to the extent that its average drift, scaled by how many flips have been read so far, matches that expectation. A long streak makes the tally run away (too much drift), and strict alternation keeps it pinned at even (too little). So the path of the tally decides the choice, not the switch rate or the final count. This follows the brief and goes after the critique's finding that the best model doesn't penalise long streaks enough.\n\n**Model:**\n- **Feature:** for each sequence, the average over positions k of |heads lead| ÷ √k.\n- **Person-level ideal drift:** each person's ideal is drawn from a log-normal population (non-centred, 400 slots so new participants can be predicted).\n- **Choice:** the probability of choosing left is a sigmoid of a sensitivity parameter (β) times the difference between the two sequences' squared distances from the person's ideal.\n\n**Self-check warnings:**\n- **PSIS-LOO is unreliable on the smoke fit:** 5.2% of trials have Pareto k > 0.5, above the 1% tolerance, so the ELPD-LOO above may be inaccurate.\n- **Convergence wasn't checked:** a single chain can't report R-hat. Admission's full fit will apply the real convergence gate.\n- **Novelty isn't checked:** the check doesn't compare it against the other models. The drift measure may track switch rate closely enough to fail that check, but the tally path is a different statistic from anything in the current set.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_0/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2411,"cache_read_input_tokens":55724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2411,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8ab918b-3a22-498b-973e-99834271c375","uuid":"09b2b91c-fdae-43f1-ba0b-5cd9ac051f8a","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:15:16.986Z","request_id":"req_011CfeexSkAoi5jdAUQEZ5XL"}
